      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the usual maximum for metformin. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, while the labeled maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets (some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day). Metformin is also not typically given as 1700 mg per dose, since the usual tablet strengths are 500, 850, and 1000 mg.\n\nThis may be a transcription error, such as 500 mg or 850 mg, or a mistaken frequency. Please have the prescribing physician confirm the intended dose with the medicine team before anything is entered. Orders for patients also need to come from a licensed prescriber.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a specific corrected dose, they can give it to me and I'll enter it. I'd need the drug, the dose in mg, the route, and the number of doses per day. The order can also include a note recording the prescriber's confirmation."
      }
